{# Variables: paper (Paper), passages (list[{paper_id, section, score, text}]) #}
{# Produces: JSON matching PerPaperSummary schema #}
You are analyzing a single academic paper.

PAPER:
- Title: "{{ paper.title | replace('"', "'") }}"
- Authors: {{ paper.authors | join(", ") }}
- Year: {{ paper.year or "unknown" }}
- Paper ID: {{ paper.paper_id }}

RETRIEVED PASSAGES FROM THIS PAPER (use as your sole source of truth):
{% for p in passages %}
[P{{ paper.paper_id }}-{{ loop.index }}] (section={{ p.section or "unknown" }}, score={{ "%.3f"|format(p.score) }})
{{ p.text }}
{% endfor %}

TASK: Produce a structured summary. Every claim MUST cite at least one passage.
Use the bracketed marker format EXACTLY as shown: [P{{ paper.paper_id }}-N].

OUTPUT: STRICT JSON conforming to PerPaperSummary with fields:
  - paper_id: "{{ paper.paper_id }}"
  - objective: {text, citations: [...]}   (1-2 sentence objective)
  - methodology: {text, citations: [...]}  (2-4 sentence methodology)
  - findings: [{text, citations: [...]}, ...]   (2-5 bullet findings)
  - limitations: [{text, citations: [...]}, ...] (1-4 bullet limitations)
If a section cannot be supported from the passages, emit "[NOT IN PASSAGES]" in text.
